{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2268","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. KiaKio and Energy Intervals"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Kia and Kio found a glowing array $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ inside a crystal terminal in the ruins of an ancient digital kingdom."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The terminal works like this. Kia picks a segment of the array: any two indices $$$l$$$ and $$$r$$$ with $$$l \\lt r$$$ (so the segment always has at least two elements). Kio then finds the strongest energy in that segment, $$$m = \\max\\left(a_l, a_{l+1}, \\ldots, a_r\\right)$$$, and the terminal masks every element of the segment with $$$m$$$ (bitwise AND), then fuses the results together (bitwise XOR):"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$$$$ (a_l \\,\\&\\, m)\\oplus(a_{l+1} \\,\\&\\, m)\\oplus\\cdots\\oplus(a_r \\,\\&\\, m). $$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"That number is the energy released."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Kia wants the strongest possible blast. Over all valid segments $$$(l, r)$$$, what is the largest energy the terminal can produce?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Here, $$$\\&$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#AND"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise AND"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" operation, and $$$\\oplus$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#XOR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise XOR"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" operation."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$). The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 2\\cdot10^5$$$) — the size of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$$$ ($$$0 \\le a_i \\lt 2^{18}$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2\\cdot10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print a single integer — the maximum possible value of"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$$$$ (a_l \\,\\&\\, m)\\oplus(a_{l+1} \\,\\&\\, m)\\oplus\\cdots\\oplus(a_r \\,\\&\\, m) $$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"among all pairs $$$(l,r)$$$ satisfying $$$l \\lt r$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n5\n1 7 3 7 2\n3\n3 1 2\n5\n1 5 2 3 4\n4\n3 5 2 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n2\n5\n5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, one optimal interval is $$$l=1$$$ and $$$r=2$$$. The maximum element in this interval is $$$m=7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The value becomes $$$(1\\,\\& \\,7)\\oplus(7\\,\\&\\,7) = 6$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"2268C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2268/problem/C"}